{"validity":"pass","quality":"adequate","issues":[{"kind":"annotation","location":"design.roles.priya_user (facts) and obligations.priya_channel_reactions.scope","problem":"Priya's channel memberships are listed as C_INFRA, C_MODEL, C_GROWTH, C06ALPHADEV, but the base seed's channel_members table also shows U_PRIYA as a member of C_FRONTEND. The obligation's scope text further narrows to only C_INFRA/C_MODEL/C_GROWTH, silently dropping both C06ALPHADEV and C_FRONTEND from the stated qualifying set. Since C_FRONTEND already has real messages authored by real users (Aisha, Mateo, Łukasz) in the base seed, this is a preexisting channel that should be recognized as part of the qualifying scope for the requested route (any channel where Priya holds conversation membership).","repair":"Update the priya_user role facts to list all five channels (including C_FRONTEND) and correct the obligation scope wording to state the full membership-derived channel set (or explicitly note that C06ALPHADEV/C_FRONTEND currently have no reactions), so the enumerated scope matches the actual base seed and does not risk being read as an intentional narrowing of the request."}],"rationale":"The route (REACTION→MESSAGE→CONVERSATION→CONVERSATION_MEMBERSHIP) correctly operationalizes 'reactions on messages in channels Priya belongs to,' and the match/negative roles are semantically sound: the engineering-channel reaction is correctly excluded (Priya not a member there), and the same-named-but-different 'growth' channel (C04MNOP3456) is correctly distinguished from C_GROWTH as a negative despite the superficial name match. Planned new reaction rows (matches and negatives) not yet in the base seed are acceptable per design-stage conventions. However, the design's enumeration of Priya's memberships (missing C_FRONTEND, a real preexisting membership with real messages) and the obligation's scope text (dropping C06ALPHADEV and C_FRONTEND) do not fully match the base seed's channel_members table, creating a documentation gap that could mislead compilation about the true qualifying channel set, even though no currently-listed match/negative role is invalidated by it. This is a fixable annotation issue rather than a structural validity failure, and answer_attributes/task/obligations are otherwise well-formed and API-discoverable via conversations.members, users.conversations, conversations.history, and reactions.get."}
